Significance: minor
Type: added

Add an Uninstall settings screen that controls what deleting the plugin removes. Every option is off by default, so deleting GatherPress keeps your data unless you ask for it to go. You can opt in separately to removing events, RSVPs, topics, venues, generated files, scheduled jobs, per-user preferences, and the plugin settings. The choices never travel in a settings export and an import will not set them. The Plugins screen says so in the GatherPress row when anything is selected, so the consequence is beside the Delete link that triggers it. On multisite a network administrator can answer once for every site or leave each site to answer for its own data.
